WEBVTT

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.780
Initiating Minovsky
particle broadcast!

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.170
Everyone! Get ready!

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.010
<i>Karen!</i>

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.710
<i>Point Charlie,</i>
<i>sighted and locked!</i>

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.140
Michel! Aim well!

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.350
<i>Aye, sir.</i>

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.360
Raise output on beam weaponry.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.410
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.290
I'm not going to die!

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.390
<i>Passing point Alpha!</i>
<i>I only see the monster.</i>

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.830
<i>Raise the balloons!</i>

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:17.990
<i>Michel!</i>

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:42.950
MICHEL!!!

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.410
<i>Let go of me!</i>
<i>Do you want to get killed?!</i>

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:16.550
That voice... It can't be!

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:23.520
<i>COMMANDER!</i>

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:27.300
God dammit! I lost it!

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:31.430
It can't be... Shiro...
Where did he go?!

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.100
SHIRO!!!

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:56.690
<i>Universal Century 0079.</i>

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.830
<i>The war begun by the</i>
<i>Principality of Zeon in their bid...</i>

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.630
<i>...for independence from</i>
<i>the Earth Federation...</i>

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.930
<i>...had entered a new</i>
<i>phase thanks to...</i>

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.600
<i>...the recently fought</i>
<i>Operation Odessa.</i>

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:13.280
<i>Amidst all that, I had gone to</i>
<i>the Federal Forces Kojima base...</i>

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:17.680
<i>...in the Asian sector for data</i>
<i>on a new Zeon mobile armor.</i>

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.470
Commander Miller. I've brought
Ensign Shiro Amada for you.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.120
I can see why Commander Kojima's
complained so much.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:58.450
Recovering this thing must have
taken a helluva lot of work.

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:09.400
I'm Alice Miller.
Intelligence division.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.370
Shiro Amada.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.100
Jacob!

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.200
What do you think
you're doing?

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:19.370
Get him out of those!
You're insulting the ensign!

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.340
B- But, ma'am...

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.780
JACOB!

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:23.770
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:46.000
Do you take it black?

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:48.000
Yeah... Thank you.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:57.340
So, ten days ago, you
encountered this mobile armor...

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:59.980
...at the testing grounds
in area 5-2-6.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.180
And then, during the battle,
you vanished before the eyes...

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.220
...of the other members
of the 08th Team.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:08.290
4 hours later, a distress
signal was sent out.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.990
12 hours after that,
you were recovered safely...

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.590
...in the mountains
in area 8-4-7.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:17.600
Right.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:22.430
However, we've spotted a
few questionable things...

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.630
...in what supposedly
happened in that time.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:33.010
The result being that you're
now suspected of being a spy.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.920
They think you
wanted to hand over...

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:44.660
...a highly classified Gundam
from the very start...

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.770
...and deliberately contacted
that mobile armor.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:55.330
You successfully vanished from your
team during a chaotic battle...

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:59.140
...but then an unexpected accident
occurred while you were en route...

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:02.440
...forcing you down into area
8-4-7. You called for help.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:05.650
But then a Federal
Forces rescue team...

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.880
...showed up at the
same time as the Zeon.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.790
They were forced to self-
destruct the new mobile armor.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:14.390
And, in the end, you were
abandoned by the enemy...

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.430
...to be rescued by our forces.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:21.090
Or that's the line of reasoning
the higher-ups are following.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.690
Ridiculous!

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.190
I completely agree.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.710
They're letting their
imaginations run away with them.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:36.570
However, it's not so easy
to change their minds.

00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:45.290
That's why I want
your cooperation.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.360
Cooperation?

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:53.130
Won't you tell me?
What really happened?

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.720
So you can prove
your innocence.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:59.140
My... innocence...

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:04.270
Now tell me.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:05.870
The truth.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:13.150
What really happened on
that day in area 8-4-7?

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:19.320
I was... We were...
trapped in a blizzard.

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.590
"We"?

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:25.620
You mean with
the Zeon pilot?

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.390
Yeah.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:30.830
And it was a woman, right?

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:32.970
Yeah...

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:36.440
A woman named Aina.
Aina Sahalin.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:40.500
How do you know that?

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:47.110
Your teammates told me.
So, who is Aina Sahalin?

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:53.720
Hey, you!

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.490
God dammit!

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:13.570
<i>All this is doing</i>
<i>is using up my air!</i>

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:15.670
<i>What have I got to lose now?!</i>

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.390
I will not be a prisoner
of the Federal Forces.

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:38.200
Shoot me now.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.200
C'mon. Can you stand up?

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.710
Don't touch me!

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:49.200
- Is it deep?
- It's just a scratch!

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:53.980
Here.

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:57.410
Christ...

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:01.590
What did I do
to deserve this?

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.890
Why are you helping me?

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:07.520
I don't know, either!

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.030
But nobody's an "ally" or an
"enemy" in this situation!

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.870
I'm going down there.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.910
For what?

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.670
Well, to fight, of course.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:25.680
But, I think, if I go there,
I'll learn something.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:30.550
Who I am and what
I'm capable of.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:33.750
So there's no way
I can die here!

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.320
You're...

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:39.520
You're not how I pictured
a Feddie soldier would be.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.190
I envy you.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.240
Envy me?

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:53.710
Those are Zeon suits!

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.410
Let's go!

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:57.850
I don't want
to be a prisoner.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:01.480
But, if you stay here!
I can't just let you die!

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:03.520
I'll be rescued, too.

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:04.450
But!

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.490
Get going!

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.720
My name is Aina Sahalin!

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.660
Aina? My name's Shiro Amada.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:13.700
Goodbye, Shiro.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:25.970
Who would have thought
we'd meet again like that?

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:28.910
Coincidence. Or maybe fate?

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:33.740
For the two of you to meet
again in battle like that?

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:37.420
We happened to be
on the same battlefield.

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:42.190
She was the pilot of that prototype
mobile armor we were after...

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:50.030
It can't!

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.870
Can Aina be the pilot
of this monster?

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:57.300
I've gotta make sure!

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.610
Aina! Aina Sahalin!
Do you read me?!

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:04.270
Aina, I know it's you!
Answer me!

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:38.080
This is...
Anti-personnel weaponry.

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:44.720
<i>Is the pilot not using it</i>
<i>because it's Aina in there?</i>

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:51.460
<i>Or is it because</i>
<i>they're dead?</i>

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:15.720
Aina!
Aina Sahalin, right?!

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:22.190
Don't you remember?!
It's me, Shiro Amada!

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:25.930
If you're alive,
then answer me!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:42.980
It really is!
It really is Shiro Amada!

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:46.180
So, you remember me.
I'm glad you're okay.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.910
I didn't think I'd
ever see you again.

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.180
Same here.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:01.260
We may have been fighting
each other up till now...

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:04.300
...but unless we work together,
we're not going to survive.

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:22.220
I can't maintain equilibrium!

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.930
<i>Shiro, do you read me?!</i>

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.400
<i>At this rate, we're both</i>
<i>going to die! Please!</i>

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:45.430
No! Live or die,
we're doing it together!

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:49.070
You are so!

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:55.020
Besides... There's still hope!

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:57.450
C'MON!!!

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:11.860
49... 48... 47... 46...
Do I have enough propellant?!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.670
Not yet!

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:46.800
That's enough! Save yourself!

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:48.270
<i>Not yet!</i>

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:52.500
<i>It's hopeless!</i>

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.100
Are we all right?

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:27.270
SHIRO!!!!

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:57.570
It's no use...

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:05.240
I'm so tired...

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:48.780
ZEON!!!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.860
Shiro!

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:05.440
Your hands are frostbitten.
Please try not to use them.

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:10.310
I wish we could heat up some
water and warm them up slowly.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:14.210
I... I'm sorry. I...

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:21.080
Shiro?

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:25.090
Please come inside
the snow cave.

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:28.460
What happened before...
Don't worry about it!

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:33.040
I... I hate the Zeon!

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:38.570
But ever since that
day we met in space...

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:40.610
...I haven't been able
to forget about you.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:44.940
Even though you're Zeon.

00:17:45.180 --> 00:17:47.510
Even though you've
got a boyfriend.

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:49.550
A boyfriend?

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:58.020
I don't have a boyfriend.

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:02.620
And even though you're
a Feddie, my answer is...

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:08.870
Aina...

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:28.310
Okay, do it!

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:40.030
Whew! Even at the lowest setting,
this thing really packs a wallop!

00:18:43.210 --> 00:18:45.370
Using a beam weapon
to heat the water...

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:49.640
You really get
some strange ideas!

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:01.460
My hands are
all pins and needles.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:04.860
Hang in there. That means your
blood is starting to flow again.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.660
My feet are going numb.

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:10.670
Say, you want in
on the bath here?

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:25.540
You can look now.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.410
Whew! My heart is
beating so fast!

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:32.150
So is mine.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:53.270
I wish we could just be the
last man and woman in the world...

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:07.880
Someday... We'll meet again.

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:16.700
Why?

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:23.170
There's no reason to fight!

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:27.880
<i>Have sighted enemy prototype!</i>

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:33.220
This is the war
we're fighting...

00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:40.320
STOP IT!!!

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:44.550
Are you trying
to kill yourself?!

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.220
Aina, tell me!

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:51.860
If this is war, is there
no hope at all for US?!

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:05.240
I see.

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:08.340
But was that the
right decision to make?

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:17.350
If you'd killed her, we could have
recovered the mobile armor intact.

00:22:18.190 --> 00:22:21.560
Even so, I!

00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:25.020
You chose not to do so.

00:22:26.530 --> 00:22:29.620
Well, either way, your
situation isn't that good.

00:22:30.130 --> 00:22:34.400
You see, you let an enemy
right in front of you...

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:36.840
...escape not once but twice.

00:22:39.010 --> 00:22:43.910
I just... I just wanted to
avoid any unnecessary deaths.

00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:46.680
No, that's not true.

00:22:47.780 --> 00:22:50.950
You're in love. With that woman.

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:56.450
That's right...
I'm in love with her.

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:09.900
So, assuming all
that was the truth...

00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:13.340
...what's the best way for
me to write it in my report?

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:23.750
<i>Now then, we will</i>
<i>begin this inquiry...</i>

00:23:23.820 --> 00:23:26.550
<i>...into the conduct</i>
<i>of Ensign Shiro Amada.</i>

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:30.320
<i>You are suspected</i>
<i>of being a spy!</i>

00:23:32.060 --> 00:23:34.550
Looks like the
inquiry's started.

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:37.530
Yeah, I know.

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:40.330
I guess because you
can't go anywhere now...

00:23:40.400 --> 00:23:42.370
...without hearing rumors
about our commander.

00:23:43.110 --> 00:23:46.510
That intel spook questioned
me again yesterday.

00:23:47.210 --> 00:23:49.140
They debriefed me, too.

00:23:50.010 --> 00:23:53.410
God, what are the
higher-ups thinking?!

00:23:53.480 --> 00:23:56.880
Well, it's hard to believe.
That the commander's a spy...

00:23:57.220 --> 00:23:59.190
You little! What do
you mean by that?!

00:24:00.420 --> 00:24:03.090
Don't tell me you actually
bought that load of crap!

00:24:03.730 --> 00:24:05.090
The commander...

00:24:05.160 --> 00:24:08.720
The commander's always
honest to himself!

00:24:08.930 --> 00:24:12.030
That time in space, when I
was cornered by the enemy...

00:24:12.100 --> 00:24:15.270
...he put himself
in danger to save me!

00:24:15.870 --> 00:24:19.240
That's not the sort of
thing an enemy spy would do!

00:24:19.880 --> 00:24:24.210
Y- Yeah, that's right!
Don't you think so, too, Karen?

00:24:24.610 --> 00:24:28.520
I'm not as in love with
that newbie as Sanders is.

00:24:28.590 --> 00:24:31.180
Still, there's that
stuff he always says...

00:24:31.620 --> 00:24:32.920
"Come back alive."

00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:35.460
"I'll do what it takes to
keep you alive!" you mean?

00:24:36.790 --> 00:24:39.660
It's a happy man
who can not only...

00:24:39.730 --> 00:24:42.960
...say something that naive
but actually live by it as well.

00:24:44.300 --> 00:24:48.430
I think being a spy would be
too hard for a guy like that.

00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:53.580
Y- Yeah, exactly! It's crazy
to suspect the commander!

00:24:54.380 --> 00:24:57.640
No matter what happens,
I'll believe in him!

00:24:58.350 --> 00:24:59.980
Getting carried
away, are we?

00:25:06.020 --> 00:25:09.930
Besides that... When she hears
what's happened to the commander...

00:25:09.990 --> 00:25:12.330
Poor Kiki will be so upset...

00:25:13.130 --> 00:25:15.560
Oh, that guerrilla girl, huh?

00:25:16.330 --> 00:25:21.070
She's really fallen for him, too.
I feel sorta sorry for her.

00:25:22.140 --> 00:25:23.700
Hm? Why's that?

00:25:24.780 --> 00:25:30.210
Well, the Zeon pilot who helped
him on the mountain was named Aina.

00:25:30.750 --> 00:25:33.110
That's a woman's name, right?

00:25:34.450 --> 00:25:35.710
What did you say?

00:25:35.790 --> 00:25:37.280
That's news to me.

00:25:37.350 --> 00:25:38.980
Who told you that?

00:25:39.060 --> 00:25:44.320
Huh? Didn't you hear it during the
battle in the testing grounds?

00:25:47.330 --> 00:25:49.760
Did you tell anyone about that?!

00:25:50.500 --> 00:25:52.760
Don't tell anyone! At all!

00:25:54.570 --> 00:25:56.560
Because if you DO tell anyone...

00:25:59.810 --> 00:26:01.640
You're dead!

00:26:04.050 --> 00:26:08.850
C- C'mon, Karen. I didn't
MEAN to tell them, but...

00:26:20.800 --> 00:26:23.960
Even though we are divided
into "enemy" and "ally"...

00:26:24.030 --> 00:26:26.090
...there are good
people on both sides.

00:26:26.170 --> 00:26:28.140
We can understand each other!

00:26:28.510 --> 00:26:32.410
And for me, knowing that amidst
the stupidity of this war...

00:26:33.510 --> 00:26:36.170
...is the one thing
that gives me hope!

00:26:51.060 --> 00:26:54.360
<i>Ensign, may I ask</i>
<i>you one question?</i>

00:26:56.530 --> 00:26:59.830
<i>Feeling as you do, can you</i>
<i>still fire at the enemy?</i>

00:27:00.570 --> 00:27:02.060
I think...

00:27:16.150 --> 00:27:17.810
I think...

00:27:20.460 --> 00:27:22.930
I think I still don't know.

00:27:25.360 --> 00:27:27.760
<i>This inquiry is concluded.</i>

00:27:28.270 --> 00:27:31.200
<i>Ensign Shiro Amada, pending</i>
<i>the decision of this tribunal...</i>

00:27:31.270 --> 00:27:36.730
<i>...you are confined to quarters.</i>
<i>These proceedings are now closed!</i>

00:27:39.740 --> 00:27:42.910
I really enjoyed that little
sermon you gave before!

00:27:52.360 --> 00:27:54.760
"We can understand each other."

00:27:55.430 --> 00:27:58.190
There was once another
person who said that.

00:27:59.730 --> 00:28:02.320
What do you think
happened to them?

00:28:04.030 --> 00:28:08.030
They took pity on the enemy, let
the enemy take advantage of them...

00:28:08.810 --> 00:28:11.370
...and before they knew it,
they ended up dead.

00:28:14.510 --> 00:28:17.380
Soldiers on the battlefield
are all like that.

00:28:18.050 --> 00:28:19.520
Is that a warning?

00:28:19.580 --> 00:28:21.550
Don't put your faith
in that enemy woman.

00:28:21.620 --> 00:28:24.090
Using women is a
common Zeon trick.

00:28:24.820 --> 00:28:27.150
You're infected.

00:28:27.220 --> 00:28:30.220
Infected by a disease
common to newbies like you.

00:29:01.730 --> 00:29:06.390
Amateurs. Trying to
camouflage themselves? Dell!

00:29:06.460 --> 00:29:07.260
<i>Yeah?</i>

00:29:07.330 --> 00:29:09.300
We're going to move into...

00:29:09.370 --> 00:29:11.390
<i>...that village up there</i>
<i>to get some food.</i>

00:29:11.470 --> 00:29:13.940
<i>You take the new guy and</i>
<i>swing around from the bridge.</i>

00:29:15.140 --> 00:29:18.540
<i>You understand, Arth?</i>
<i>We're not here to cause trouble.</i>

00:29:20.710 --> 00:29:24.880
Quit showing off how smart you
are and get us something to eat!

00:29:25.320 --> 00:29:26.870
Commander...

00:29:28.290 --> 00:29:31.080
You clear on this?
No killing!

00:29:31.790 --> 00:29:33.450
<i>Clear as crystal!</i>

00:29:52.840 --> 00:29:54.140
Don't.

00:29:54.210 --> 00:29:55.800
Not yet.

00:29:56.280 --> 00:29:57.710
You can't come into the fields!

00:30:15.370 --> 00:30:18.560
<i>Why's she wasting so much</i>
<i>time on this two-bit village?!</i>

00:30:21.740 --> 00:30:23.800
I'll help 'em
make up their minds...

00:30:24.710 --> 00:30:26.300
<i>Whoops!</i>

00:30:35.520 --> 00:30:36.450
Arth!

00:30:39.190 --> 00:30:42.520
Sorry! We didn't mean
to cause any trouble.

00:30:44.900 --> 00:30:48.420
We were just hoping you'd
share some food with us.

00:30:48.930 --> 00:30:51.660
Well, then, keep that
monster of yours back!

00:30:51.740 --> 00:30:53.670
You coulda just said
so to start with!

00:30:54.770 --> 00:30:57.930
We're on the run.
Trust doesn't come easy.

00:30:58.510 --> 00:31:01.600
Hmpf! Well, we don't
have much to share...

00:31:02.150 --> 00:31:04.010
WE'VE got the mobile suits.

00:31:04.080 --> 00:31:05.910
Why are we letting
these guys insult us?

00:31:10.550 --> 00:31:13.150
God, can you believe this rain?

00:31:14.220 --> 00:31:17.250
Hey, Pops! Vodka!
Bring the whole bottle here!

00:31:18.130 --> 00:31:20.960
And forget the ice.
The weather's too cold for that.

00:31:21.700 --> 00:31:24.030
So, your commander's
a Zeek spy.

00:31:24.100 --> 00:31:26.070
Must be tough for the
08th Team right now.

00:31:26.970 --> 00:31:30.600
The commander... wouldn't
do something like that.

00:31:31.170 --> 00:31:33.510
Well, it's gotten
you some free time.

00:31:33.580 --> 00:31:35.810
You can enjoy yourselves
all afternoon in the bar.

00:31:35.880 --> 00:31:37.140
You've got nothing
to complain about.

00:31:40.750 --> 00:31:43.350
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Relax, friend.

00:31:43.420 --> 00:31:45.450
I'm worn out enough!

00:31:45.520 --> 00:31:48.550
Why don't I tell you something
interesting instead?

00:31:49.630 --> 00:31:52.460
The village where your
guerrilla buddies are?

00:31:52.530 --> 00:31:54.190
The Zeon are attacking it.

00:31:54.800 --> 00:31:56.490
Kiki's village?!

00:31:57.070 --> 00:31:59.730
Well, did they fight?!
Is Kiki okay?!

00:32:00.370 --> 00:32:02.340
I don't know any details.

00:32:02.410 --> 00:32:06.210
The underground sonar just
told us that they're there.

00:32:06.280 --> 00:32:10.040
You mean... Why isn't
anyone checking it out?!

00:32:11.050 --> 00:32:15.280
I reported it. They'll order
someone out if they need to.

00:32:15.850 --> 00:32:18.480
Someone besides YOU GUYS.

00:32:21.360 --> 00:32:24.120
Thanks for your
valuable information.

00:32:24.190 --> 00:32:26.420
Here's a drink
for you, my treat.

00:32:27.560 --> 00:32:29.330
I'll tell the commander!

00:32:30.630 --> 00:32:32.470
It looks like Commander
Kojima doesn't think...

00:32:32.540 --> 00:32:34.270
...it's worth
sending anyone out.

00:32:34.710 --> 00:32:36.300
He said...

00:32:36.370 --> 00:32:38.930
Protecting the guerrillas
wasn't our responsibility.

00:32:39.840 --> 00:32:41.400
I figured telling
you about it...

00:32:41.480 --> 00:32:44.450
...while you're under confinement
would be tough on you, but...

00:32:44.510 --> 00:32:47.310
But I prefer that to
not knowing about it.

00:32:47.380 --> 00:32:50.650
You understand, don't you?
You could all be court-martialed.

00:32:51.190 --> 00:32:53.250
Court-martialed?!

00:32:53.820 --> 00:32:56.350
We won't get executed, right?

00:32:57.160 --> 00:32:59.420
We can't just abandon friends.

00:32:59.500 --> 00:33:03.660
I have to pay them back for those
great sandwiches they brought us.

00:33:05.770 --> 00:33:08.600
Well, I just want
to go help Kiki!

00:33:08.970 --> 00:33:11.840
All right, as your
team leader, I order you!

00:33:12.440 --> 00:33:14.310
08th Team, move out!

00:33:14.380 --> 00:33:15.350
Aye, sir!

00:33:15.410 --> 00:33:17.440
Not so fast!

00:33:18.720 --> 00:33:22.150
If you three obey his order...

00:33:22.220 --> 00:33:25.480
...the newbie here will
take all the blame.

00:33:26.060 --> 00:33:26.890
But...

00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:29.150
So I suggest you use THIS!

00:33:29.990 --> 00:33:31.590
An orders form!

00:33:31.660 --> 00:33:34.150
With Kojima's
signature on it?!

00:33:34.230 --> 00:33:36.500
I'll let you
have it real cheap!

00:33:37.770 --> 00:33:38.460
Let's go!

00:33:38.540 --> 00:33:39.900
Listen, kid!

00:33:39.970 --> 00:33:42.910
You can't just keep going
head-on against the world.

00:33:43.610 --> 00:33:48.570
There are times you need to use the
backdoors to get public support.

00:33:49.050 --> 00:33:51.340
I'm sorry, Old Man...

00:33:51.720 --> 00:33:53.910
That's a step I'm
not ready to take yet.

00:33:56.020 --> 00:33:59.480
Typical newbie.
Put it on my tab.

00:34:00.290 --> 00:34:02.320
We'll pay you back for this.

00:34:02.730 --> 00:34:04.220
We owe you.

00:34:05.460 --> 00:34:07.900
Nothing but trouble...

00:34:08.470 --> 00:34:10.930
You'll never
be good soldiers...

00:34:20.440 --> 00:34:23.410
<i>If we're going up</i>
<i>against mobile suits...</i>

00:34:24.010 --> 00:34:27.350
<i>...why are we waiting so</i>
<i>far from the village?</i>

00:34:27.980 --> 00:34:29.350
Dunno.

00:34:29.920 --> 00:34:32.390
<i>The commander must</i>
<i>have some kind of plan.</i>

00:34:34.460 --> 00:34:37.050
Well, we'll see how clever he is.

00:34:42.530 --> 00:34:45.660
<i>Can you do that? You just</i>
<i>have anti-tank weapons.</i>

00:34:47.840 --> 00:34:50.500
Pilots know how pilots fight.

00:34:51.740 --> 00:34:56.040
Thanks. Once you
secure the comm line here...

00:34:56.110 --> 00:34:57.770
...stand by in the hovertruck.

00:34:57.850 --> 00:35:01.440
Commander!
It's about the inquiry...

00:35:01.520 --> 00:35:05.650
Look... This isn't worth
killing yourself over.

00:35:07.090 --> 00:35:09.620
Please, give the order
you always give!

00:35:09.690 --> 00:35:11.850
About everyone coming
back in one piece.

00:35:12.430 --> 00:35:14.160
<i>Here's your food!</i>

00:35:14.230 --> 00:35:17.600
She's a little young,
but beggars can't be choosers.

00:35:28.410 --> 00:35:30.110
<i>Arth! Stop it!</i>

00:35:32.920 --> 00:35:35.210
<i>You wouldn't shoot me.</i>

00:35:35.750 --> 00:35:37.980
I'll say you were
killed in action.

00:35:40.120 --> 00:35:43.020
All right,
I'll put her down.

00:35:44.790 --> 00:35:47.390
I'll just take my food, first.

00:35:47.800 --> 00:35:49.420
You son of a!

00:35:52.870 --> 00:35:55.060
- Miss Kiki!
- No, don't!

00:35:57.110 --> 00:36:00.370
We can't risk turning the village
into a battlefield just for revenge!

00:36:01.040 --> 00:36:02.670
Wait for our chance!

00:36:04.310 --> 00:36:06.180
Serves her right!

00:36:09.020 --> 00:36:10.580
You're dead.

00:36:17.390 --> 00:36:18.860
It's begun!

00:36:18.930 --> 00:36:20.230
Dammit!

00:36:22.300 --> 00:36:25.430
Is this maximum
magnification? God dammit...

00:36:29.840 --> 00:36:33.300
That idiot!
It was too soon!

00:36:34.010 --> 00:36:35.740
Now we can't
let the others go!

00:36:40.350 --> 00:36:42.280
They're guerrillas!

00:36:42.820 --> 00:36:45.980
Oh, we picked a fine place
to stop for a meal!

00:36:46.460 --> 00:36:49.360
<i>Dell! No point staying now!</i>
<i>Let's get out of here!</i>

00:36:49.430 --> 00:36:51.330
<i>Roger! Is Arth?</i>

00:36:51.760 --> 00:36:54.990
<i>Forget him! I'll cover you!</i>
<i>Can you jump?</i>

00:36:56.830 --> 00:36:59.670
<i>Yeah! I should be</i>
<i>able to manage one!</i>

00:37:00.200 --> 00:37:01.640
You're not gettin' away!

00:37:02.510 --> 00:37:04.030
Behind me?!

00:37:20.260 --> 00:37:22.520
Dammit! They're not
gonna let us escape!

00:37:24.630 --> 00:37:25.650
Are you okay?!

00:37:25.730 --> 00:37:29.130
Shiro... You're alive...

00:37:31.530 --> 00:37:33.060
Where am I?!

00:37:33.900 --> 00:37:36.530
In danger. Can you move?

00:37:42.180 --> 00:37:44.980
The cyclops?! What happened?!

00:37:45.050 --> 00:37:46.850
My house!

00:37:47.920 --> 00:37:51.790
Dad... Daddy!!!

00:37:58.700 --> 00:38:00.530
What's wrong with them?!

00:38:00.600 --> 00:38:04.120
If they don't let us go, their
village'll become a battlefield!

00:38:04.630 --> 00:38:06.190
You're not getting away!

00:38:07.100 --> 00:38:09.070
Get the women and children
out of the village!

00:38:09.140 --> 00:38:11.940
Anyone who can fight,
drive them towards the river!

00:38:12.440 --> 00:38:15.310
The river?! Do you WANT
them to get away?!

00:38:15.780 --> 00:38:18.040
At this rate,
the village'll be destroyed!

00:38:19.120 --> 00:38:21.880
It doesn't matter,
as long as we pay them back!

00:38:21.950 --> 00:38:24.780
Those enemy pilots are
desperate to stay alive, too!

00:38:24.850 --> 00:38:27.690
What the hell does a Fed
newbie know about this?!

00:38:27.760 --> 00:38:30.690
We won't stop till
they're all dead!

00:38:33.100 --> 00:38:35.330
Kiki, do you feel
the same way?

00:38:35.400 --> 00:38:38.930
I want to get them
back for my dad!

00:38:39.370 --> 00:38:43.400
Yeah! Fight them!
Kill 'em all! Smash the enemy!

00:38:43.470 --> 00:38:46.070
Look, maybe this is
"youthful idealism"...

00:38:46.880 --> 00:38:50.640
...but I want to save those
guys in the Zakus, too!

00:38:54.880 --> 00:38:57.650
What the hell is
he babbling about?

00:38:57.720 --> 00:38:59.480
Shiro...

00:39:00.760 --> 00:39:03.950
<i>Karen! Sanders!</i>
<i>Stand by with the beam rifles!</i>

00:39:42.700 --> 00:39:44.290
FIRE!!!

00:39:47.970 --> 00:39:49.460
<i>Commander!</i>

00:39:52.310 --> 00:39:54.110
Beam weaponry?!

00:39:57.410 --> 00:40:00.470
<i>Sanders, correct 0.2</i>
<i>degrees to the right!</i>

00:40:16.170 --> 00:40:18.430
There's no reason
to fight anymore!

00:40:18.700 --> 00:40:21.570
<i>Surrender! We'll let you live!</i>

00:40:24.170 --> 00:40:25.940
They got Dell, too?

00:40:26.580 --> 00:40:27.840
Those idiot guerrillas!

00:40:44.830 --> 00:40:46.300
Surrender!

00:40:55.270 --> 00:40:56.800
Stop it! Don't!

00:41:02.080 --> 00:41:03.740
Anti-personnel weapons!

00:41:04.910 --> 00:41:06.310
Get back!

00:41:13.920 --> 00:41:15.250
That's enough!

00:41:17.560 --> 00:41:18.860
I'll finish you!

00:41:18.930 --> 00:41:21.830
STOP THIS, PLEASE!!!

00:41:24.230 --> 00:41:26.930
<i>Can you still</i>
<i>fire at the enemy?</i>

00:41:41.820 --> 00:41:45.780
Forging orders and going out on
an attack while under house arrest...

00:41:46.820 --> 00:41:49.790
There's no way we're going
to avoid a court-martial now.

00:41:49.860 --> 00:41:53.890
I admit that I disobeyed
orders, sir. However...

00:41:55.700 --> 00:41:59.860
I am convinced that our
attack was justified!

00:42:00.470 --> 00:42:02.100
You little!

00:42:07.480 --> 00:42:09.210
Very well.

00:42:10.410 --> 00:42:13.350
The fact remains that you
<i>did</i> wipe out that enemy team.

00:42:13.420 --> 00:42:14.710
We have to take
that into account.

00:42:20.020 --> 00:42:23.120
And for that...
I'm giving you...

00:42:23.190 --> 00:42:27.460
<i>All</i> of you in the 08th Team,
a chance to redeem yourselves.

00:42:29.330 --> 00:42:31.820
I want you to be airdropped...

00:42:31.900 --> 00:42:35.530
...behind enemy lines to
find their base for us.

00:42:35.610 --> 00:42:38.400
This is a vital mission
which may decide...

00:42:38.470 --> 00:42:41.770
...whether we win or lose in
the coming showdown. However...

00:42:43.080 --> 00:42:45.810
...it is also an extremely
dangerous mission.

00:42:46.280 --> 00:42:49.880
In fact, they tell me your chances
of coming back alive from it...

00:42:49.950 --> 00:42:52.110
...are only 38%.

00:42:53.790 --> 00:42:55.880
A commander who cares
about his people...

00:42:55.960 --> 00:42:58.620
...might not
accept this mission.

00:42:58.860 --> 00:43:01.090
However, if you refuse
these orders...

00:43:02.400 --> 00:43:04.030
...there's a firing squad
waiting for all of you.

00:43:11.910 --> 00:43:13.570
Good luck!

00:43:13.640 --> 00:43:15.630
Hey, wait!

00:43:15.710 --> 00:43:18.370
You're just gonna
leave me to die?!

00:43:18.450 --> 00:43:20.420
Accept it gracefully!

00:43:20.480 --> 00:43:22.610
I can spend your song's
royalties for you!

00:43:25.620 --> 00:43:28.280
- Take care now!
- See ya!

00:43:28.360 --> 00:43:31.820
YOU BASTARDS! HEY!

00:43:34.660 --> 00:43:37.630
Christ, you're pathetic.

00:43:40.570 --> 00:43:44.010
Eledore! Welcome back!

00:43:46.040 --> 00:43:47.810
Uh... Hi!

00:43:50.480 --> 00:43:52.910
So, how was life
in the hospital?

00:43:53.520 --> 00:43:55.380
It SUCKED is what it was!

00:43:56.390 --> 00:43:58.850
The whole hospital was
talking about those rumors.

00:43:59.420 --> 00:44:01.650
Of how the commander's a spy.

00:44:01.720 --> 00:44:04.720
Not just that. Is it true you
guys were his accomplices...

00:44:04.790 --> 00:44:07.190
...and pulled some
major crap, too?

00:44:08.260 --> 00:44:09.750
Sort of.

00:44:10.470 --> 00:44:12.800
Well, thanks to that, they
shipped me back to the front line...

00:44:12.870 --> 00:44:14.460
...right after I was released!

00:44:14.540 --> 00:44:17.270
You're the last people
I want to be with right now!

00:44:17.340 --> 00:44:20.640
Yeah, these new orders we got
aren't really fair, are they?

00:44:21.180 --> 00:44:24.910
Well, I prefer them to a
firing squad. Right, Sanders?

00:44:26.420 --> 00:44:27.610
Yeah...

00:44:27.680 --> 00:44:29.650
By the way, where's Newbie?

00:44:30.520 --> 00:44:32.950
There's the commander,
over there.

00:44:36.490 --> 00:44:38.550
I- It's her!

00:44:38.630 --> 00:44:40.220
The intel spook!

00:44:40.900 --> 00:44:42.590
So, you went out
and destroyed...

00:44:42.670 --> 00:44:44.630
...an enemy force
against overwhelming odds.

00:44:44.700 --> 00:44:46.600
Very skillful of you.

00:44:46.670 --> 00:44:49.260
You're a very skillful
Federal Forces officer.

00:44:49.740 --> 00:44:52.040
You did the right thing.

00:44:52.110 --> 00:44:54.910
And as a result,
you avoided execution.

00:44:54.980 --> 00:44:56.910
So why are you
so upset about it?

00:44:59.120 --> 00:45:03.180
It seems to me you have a few
misconceptions about this war.

00:45:03.720 --> 00:45:07.050
The "reformation of humanity" and
"government for the Spacenoids"...

00:45:07.120 --> 00:45:10.250
This "independence from the
Federation"...it's all just a sham!

00:45:10.330 --> 00:45:12.560
The Zeon are the worst
terrorists in history!

00:45:12.630 --> 00:45:14.620
Just animals in human skins!

00:45:15.360 --> 00:45:18.700
Yeah, and I think killing
as many of them as possible...

00:45:18.770 --> 00:45:21.740
...will put us one step closer
to purifying the human race!

00:45:22.270 --> 00:45:24.240
My thoughts haven't changed.

00:45:25.210 --> 00:45:26.540
As I thought...

00:45:26.610 --> 00:45:28.580
You're Zeon, aren't you?!

00:45:30.180 --> 00:45:32.480
Go on! Admit it!

00:45:37.590 --> 00:45:39.560
Well, too bad.

00:45:39.960 --> 00:45:41.650
I'll just have to shoot.

00:45:43.460 --> 00:45:46.950
If you're a Federation officer,
then you can swear it to me now!

00:45:47.660 --> 00:45:49.820
That you'll kill
every Zeon that you can!

00:45:50.270 --> 00:45:51.430
I can't!

00:45:52.370 --> 00:45:55.460
I'll fight the way
<i>I</i> have to fight.

00:45:55.940 --> 00:45:58.030
Until this war is over...

00:46:08.620 --> 00:46:10.110
What you said...

00:46:10.750 --> 00:46:14.350
The person who was betrayed by
the enemy they felt sorry for...

00:46:14.420 --> 00:46:16.120
It was you, wasn't it?

00:46:18.290 --> 00:46:21.630
I told you before.
She died a long time ago.

00:46:21.860 --> 00:46:23.230
Commander!

00:46:28.600 --> 00:46:30.570
Everyone, listen to me.

00:46:30.640 --> 00:46:34.670
You already know how dangerous
this mission is going to be.

00:46:35.380 --> 00:46:38.750
But we aren't just
a bunch of killers!

00:46:38.820 --> 00:46:40.410
The enemy are still people.

00:46:40.480 --> 00:46:44.720
So, while we do our duty,
try to minimize the number of victims.

00:46:44.790 --> 00:46:46.880
And come back alive!

00:46:46.960 --> 00:46:50.290
That order always comes
first and will never change!

00:47:10.010 --> 00:47:11.140
Wait!

00:47:11.710 --> 00:47:15.450
You're lucky. I missed.

00:47:16.550 --> 00:47:18.610
I'm going to prove it to you.

00:47:18.690 --> 00:47:20.920
That my way of
thinking isn't wrong.

00:47:22.060 --> 00:47:25.190
Ensign, your
determination is admirable...

00:47:25.260 --> 00:47:29.290
...but the enemy you face
is now the entire world.

00:47:31.630 --> 00:47:33.430
08th Team, move out!

00:48:16.840 --> 00:48:20.370
<b><i>Tatoeba donna fuuni...
After everything that's happened...</i></b>

00:48:20.370 --> 00:48:23.600
<b><i>...kanashimi o koete kita no?
...is the sadness finally behind us now?</i></b>

00:48:23.870 --> 00:48:27.330
<b><i>Awaseta shisen no naka...
In that glance that we shared...</i></b>

00:48:27.410 --> 00:48:30.400
<b><i>...omoi ga afureta.
...feelings began to overflow.</i></b>

00:48:30.910 --> 00:48:34.160
<b><i>Kakera demo kiseki demo...
The fragments and the miracles...</i></b>

00:48:34.160 --> 00:48:37.640
<b><i>Sono subete o kizami tsuketai!
I want them all engraved within me!</i></b>

00:48:38.120 --> 00:48:43.350
<b><i>Dakishimetai!
I want to embrace them all!</i></b>

00:48:44.260 --> 00:48:50.960
<b><i>Ai yori fukaku namida yori setsunaku...
It's deeper than love, more painful than tears...</i></b>

00:48:51.600 --> 00:48:58.060
<b><i>Kokoro ga ima anata o kanjite irukara.
Because I feel you in my heart now.</i></b>

00:48:58.240 --> 00:49:01.400
<b><i>Hateshinai yumemo...
These endless dreams I have...</i></b>

00:49:01.470 --> 00:49:04.930
<b><i>...yuzurenai kimochimo...
...and these feelings I can't give up...</i></b>

00:49:05.010 --> 00:49:08.200
<b><i>Mitsumeteru shinjiteru!
As I look at you, I believe in them!</i></b>

00:49:08.200 --> 00:49:11.510
<b><i>Sobani iru yo!
I'll be here at your side!</i></b>

00:49:20.130 --> 00:49:27.090
<b><i>Miageta sora e to...
Up into the stars we see overhead...</i></b>

00:49:27.570 --> 00:49:35.500
<b><i>...anata no egaku mirai ga kono negai ga tobitatsu yo!
...flies my wish for the future you've described!</i></b>

00:49:35.910 --> 00:49:41.810
<b><i>Manazashi wa eien no tobira...
A glance can be the gateway to eternity...</i></b>

00:49:42.480 --> 00:49:48.940
<b><i>...wakachi aeru nanikaga chikara ni narunara!
...when that something we share becomes the strength we need!</i></b>

00:49:49.020 --> 00:49:55.690
<b><i>Kizutsuku koto mo owaranai namida mo.
The things that hurt us and the endless tears, too.</i></b>

00:49:55.760 --> 00:50:02.600
<b><i>Oshiminaku tamerawazu daite yukou!
They're nothing to regret, so don't hesitate to embrace them all!</i></b>

00:50:03.000 --> 00:50:10.000
<b><i>Ai yori fukaku namida yori setsunaku.
It's deeper than love, more painful than tears.</i></b>

